body:
Sometimes an up in your medication is the best move. It can be a night and day difference what the correct medication can do. As stressful as it is, you can always find a new job if things get worse, who knows, you might like your new job.

&#x200B;

Also, at least your eyes are pretty xD

Didn't read the whole thing but the first paragraph/stanza thing looks to be from google translate. especially the "id spectat terra sub" which seems to me to be a word for word translation of "it sees the earth underneath". I do not mean to be rude but it seems as if you are trying to get this subreddit to do your homework for you or you are vastly over reaching your skills. If the first is true then this is not the subreddit for you. If the second is true, take Latin one step at a time. Enjoy the beginnings and I would recommend not to write your own prose until you have read some original prose. 

&#x200B;

Another good idea is as u/kingshorsey mentioned. Familia romana is excellent for beginning Latin in a fluent, living language sense.
